[hrdoucet@watcgl.waterloo.edu (Heloise Doucet) writes:]
[] 1) I am wearing armor - Dwarven Mithril Coat - it is not cursed and I can't
[] take it off. When I give the Remove Armor command and get a list of my
[] armor items, it is not there. Is this a bug or is it something I did?

you must remove your cloak first before you can remove your suit of armor.

[] 2) When I sacrifice monsters on my altar, nothing happens or it says that
[] I feel inadequate. When I pray I lose levels. I do not kill monsters that
[] do not attack me. I don't sacrifice anything in particular - anything that
[] wanders by. Also, I have got my katana from my God. Help!

stop praying so much!  this only makes your god angrier and angrier.
you need to first sacrifice enough such that you have a feeling of
reconciliation.  then praying at that point is iffy (don't do it).
continue to sacrifice (but don't starve!) until you see four-leaf
clovers.  now you can safely pray (but you should save your prayers
for emergencies) ...

[] 3) In my intrinsics it says that I aggravate monsters. Is there something
[] that you eat that will cause this? I am not wearing anything (such as a
[] ring) that specifically aggravates monsters.

poor interface, IMO.  when you eat {little-large} dogs or {kitten-large}
cats you acquire the intrinsic aggravate monster.  the logic for why
you don't get a feeling about this is beyond me.  as it is, players
simply continue to do this over and over again without a clue ...

